=== is it independent of length, or just length again? ===
  best predictor: P(skeleton) (AUC 0.725); within length terciles:
    n <= 26              n= 154  AUC 0.640  (5 agree / 149 disagree)
    26 < n <= 35         n= 119  AUC 0.674  (29 agree / 90 disagree)
    n > 35               n= 134  AUC 0.741  (8 agree / 126 disagree)

=== verdict ===
  P(skeleton) separates agreement from disagreement at AUC 0.725. If that survives the
  length check above, a single-model ensemble quantity is a usable SURROGATE for the
  three-oracle conjunction: it can enter the loop at ViennaRNA prices instead of
  ShapeKnots prices, and it explains why inverse_pf_fold's ensemble objective matters.
  Next step would be to optimise it directly and check the panel rate, NOT to believe it.
